quran[10]{c,v,t}:
  10,79,Pharaoh said: ‘Bring me every (highly) skilled magician.’
  10,80,"So, when the magicians came, Musa (Moses) said to them: ‘Throw down what you have to throw.’"
  10,81,"When they threw down (their ropes and sticks), Musa (Moses) said: ‘Whatever you have produced is magic. Allah will soon prove it to be false. Indeed, Allah does not allow the work of mischief-makers to flourish."
  10,82,"And Allah verifies the truth through His Words, though the guilty may dislike it.’"
  10,83,"But none believed in Musa (Moses) except some youths from among his people, fearing that Pharaoh and his influential people would persecute them. And Pharaoh was indeed a tyrant in the land, and he was among the transgressors."
  10,84,"And Musa (Moses) said: ‘O my people! If you have believed in Allah, put your trust in Him, if you (truly) submit (to Him).’"
  10,85,"So they said: ‘In Allah, we have put our trust. Our Lord! Do not make us subject to the persecution of the oppressors,"
  10,86,and save us through Your mercy from the disbelieving people.’
  10,87,"And We revealed to Musa (Moses) and his brother (saying): ‘Prepare some houses for your people in Egypt, and make your houses places of worship, and establish the prayer (in them) and give glad tidings to the believers.’"
  10,88,And Musa (Moses) said: ‘Our Lord! You have given Pharaoh and his influential people luxury and abundance of wealth in this worldly life (which they abuse)—Our Lord—to lead (people) astray from Your way. Our Lord! Destroy their wealth and harden their hearts so they do not believe until they see the painful punishment.’
